    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d513">

                <pb facs="0563" n="465" xml:id="pg465"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/406: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-09-08T12:00:00+08:00">September 8,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received September 8—10:55 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>789. Your 310, Sept. 7, 1 p.m.<anchor n="60" xml:id="d513-f1"/> My understanding
                    of Lampson’s instructions convinces me that it is not possible to consider
                    deferring presentation of draft now. He arrives in Nanking September 9th and
                    will present draft as he told me. I have asked Adams<anchor n="61"
                        xml:id="d513-f2"/> to read to him Department’s 310. I have asked Adams to
                    tell Lampson that I am saying to you that I understand his instructions preclude
                    postponement of presentation of draft now and that I assume Department will call
                    in Chinese Chargé d’Affaires and inform him of its knowledge of draft without
                    giving him a copy.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d513-f1" n="60" xml:id="d513-f1-content">
                <p>Quoted in telegram No. 225, September 7, to the Ambassador in Great Britain, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supra.</hi></p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d513-f2" n="61" xml:id="d513-f2-content">
                <p>Walter A. Adams, Consul at Nanking.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
